			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_569301473354104561">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c569301473354083222">UndeadBulwark</a></b>:</div><blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c569301473354075428">☢Paradoxic Gamer☢</a></b>:</div>Gonna buy it too, AI is the future, every game developer should use AI tools to vastly increase their own productivity. </blockquote>I tried AI Game Dev and holy ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ ♥♥♥♥ so much of the tedious stuff can be passed onto an AI its amazing and I am using a local model with 256k context. </blockquote>Tediuos stuff is what makes the art amazing<br><br>look at Wildwood, it took them 16 years to animate it with their hands, and it's the best stop motion movie i've watched ever and it will become a classic <br><br>Too many shortcuts lead to dry results			</div>
